 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with a pause that grows by 2 seconds before each
+retry: 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds, 20 seconds at most. When the fifth attempt times out too, the capture fails with
+`GatewayTimeout`.
+
+The pauses exist because the gateway slows down every Friday from 17:00 to 19:00, its peak. Captures used to make 3
+attempts back to back within a second, so all three landed in the same slow minute: one Friday left 58 pantry orders
+confirmed but never charged, and a payments volunteer captured them by hand from the gateway's dashboard the next
+morning. Switching gateways was ruled out, as the contract runs to December 2026. Replaying that Friday's timeouts
+against the gateway's sandbox with 5 attempts paced 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds apart, 57 of the 58 would have gone
+through.
 
 Every attempt to capture one pantry order sends the same idempotency key, the one its first attempt used. The gateway
 can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024 retries that
 drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice.
 
+## Known limits
+
+- While the gateway is slow, the member waits on the confirmation page through the retries, up to 20 seconds longer
+  than before. This was accepted as cheaper than volunteers capturing orders by hand.
+- A capture can still fail after 5 attempts, as 1 of the 58 replayed orders would have. Workaround: follow
+  [the gateway-timeout runbook](../runbooks/gateway-timeouts.md) to find it in the logs, then capture it from the
+  gateway's dashboard, as volunteers did by hand before this change.
+
